<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4879" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμάλθ-εια</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμαλθ-είη</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμαλθ-ί̆η</span></b> , ἡ, goat <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Amaltheia,</i>
			which suckled Zeus, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				49
			</span></i>: from her horn flowed whatever its possessor wished, hence
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέρας Ἀμαλθείας</span> horn <i>of
				plenty,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Anacr.
				8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phoc.
				7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				39
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>; applied to parks, etc., <i><span class="en">
				Duris
				41
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				3.68
			</span></i>, etc.; title of book, <i><span class="en">
				Gell.
				<u>Praef.</u>
				6
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμαλθ-εῖον</span></b> , τό,
			country-house of Atticus in Epirus, <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				1.16
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				18
			</span></i>.</div>
